My second ascencion.

I got it poly-less and polyself-less (and Elbereth-less). I had tried
for wishless but Rodney pounded too hard so I wished for a blessed
wand of death. For some reason, Orcus didn't have one. Well, actually
he zapped me with it, but when I pick-axed his statue, I only found a
wand of striking. His wand of death must have exploded in a
last-chance charge or was cursed and I didn't notice since I was
chasing a cokcatrice at the time.
A ring of Teleport control was handy and I decided to eat nymphs,
tengus etc. and got teleportitis.
I managed a naked AC of -4 only through priests. I killed the priest
in Minetown, then brought a conflictual cockatrice near the priest
that I found in the main dungeon, and thus the Moloch priest in the
VotD made a lot of money.
As I thought I could go on ascencion wishless, I didn't have a
T-shirt, which could have been useful. High intelligence was not
something I managed, but using a crystal ball in the elemental planes
was definitely faster than the confused scroll thing.
Rodney killed the high priest of Moloch and left a false amulet before
I even saw the true one. I went upstairs with it and found strange
that the mysterious force wouldn't hinder me, so I went back, picked
the right amulet, and got up. I managed to reach Dlv36 and then fall
back to Dlvl44 while climbing up a few times... Twice... Grrrr...
The Air elemental plane was the hardest one, but a ring of conflict
put the elementals fighting one another instead of fighting me, so I
could hurry away.
The Astral plane was cakewall. The central altar was famine's, and it
happened to be neutral. It was very easy to get through, for a change.
I just teleported Famine away 6 or 7 times.

